Restored org-member access to org-owned domains under RBAC. Members of an org that
owns a domain were locked out (404 on reads, 400 on uploads) when the domain's
``rh-org-<org_id>`` group held no roles -- the result of a ``DomainOrg`` row with a
null ``org_id`` (its create request carried no ``internal.org_id``), which skipped the
org group's role grant. A data migration backfills existing domains, deriving the org
from the team group's members and granting ``rh-org-<org_id>`` the missing roles.
Domain creation now also derives ``org_id`` from the creating user's ``rh-org-<org_id>``
membership when the request omits ``internal.org_id``, so no new null-``org_id`` domains
are produced.
The read-only ``domainorg_backfill_report`` management command previews which domains the
backfill will repair or skip (with the reason) before it runs, so the skip-set can be
reviewed and remediated ahead of enabling RBAC. The same report is also available to admins
via ``POST /api/pulp/debug/domainorg-backfill-report/``, which dispatches a task that produces
the report as a downloadable JSON file (retrievable from the task's ``profile_artifacts``),
for environments where management commands cannot be run.
